+     "old": "- **Bazel specifics.** A selection builds exactly the transitive closure of the selected tasks, nothing else is analysed. `run-many` is one Bazel invocation with all labels, so shared dependencies run once. When a selected task is a test the invocation is `bazel test` (with `--build_tests_only` only when every selected label is a test); `--skip-cache` adds `--nocache_test_results`.\n\n",
+     "new": "- **Bazel specifics.** A selection builds exactly the transitive closure of the selected tasks, nothing else is analysed. `run-many` is one Bazel invocation with all labels, so shared dependencies run once. When a selected task is a test the invocation is `bazel test` (with `--build_tests_only` only when every selected label is a test); `--skip-cache` adds `--nocache_test_results`.\n\n### 🗣️ Language and option spelling\n\n- **No default language.** The CLI never assumes a language for its help, progress and refusal texts. It takes the first source that names an offered language (`en`, `de`): `--lang=<en|de>`, `SEMIO_LANGUAGE`, `LANGUAGE` (first offered entry), the first non-empty of `LC_ALL`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LANG` (`C` and `POSIX` name none), then the operating system language list (macOS preferences, the Windows user locale; other systems state theirs in the environment). `--lang` and `SEMIO_LANGUAGE` must name an offered language; a locale that names an unoffered one is skipped. When nothing resolves, the command refuses before it starts, in English and German, and names every way to choose (for example `SEMIO_LANGUAGE=en` in CI). One module owns the rule: `🧰️framework/🔨️modules/🏃️process/🏗️build/🗣️language`.\n- **Keine Standardsprache.** Die CLI nimmt für Hilfe, Fortschritt und Ablehnungen nie eine Sprache an. Maßgeblich ist die erste Quelle, die eine angebotene Sprache (`en`, `de`) nennt: `--lang=<en|de>`, `SEMIO_LANGUAGE`, `LANGUAGE` (erster angebotener Eintrag), die erste nicht leere Variable aus `LC_ALL`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LANG` (`C` und `POSIX` nennen keine), danach die Sprachliste des Betriebssystems. Lässt sich nichts bestimmen, verweigert sich der Befehl vor dem Start auf Englisch und Deutsch und nennt alle Wege zur Auswahl (etwa `SEMIO_LANGUAGE=de` in CI).\n- **Options.** An option with a required value (`--tool`, `--workers`, `--lang`, `--configuration`, `--store`, `--output`, `--projects`, ...) may be typed as `--option value` or `--option=value`, also by its short alias; the CLI door rewrites it to `--option=value` before anything else reads it. Options with a separate or optional value and everything after `--` stay as typed. `repo <command> --help` lists, for a subcommand, only the options and examples that belong to it, followed by the notes of its operation.\n- **Temporary directories.** `repo incremental` keeps its disposable copy in the folder `sinc` of the temporary directory of the process (inside a test sandbox, the sandbox directory); pass `--root` when that path is longer than 100 characters.\n\n",
