+     "old": "        \"Every heavy repo command (run, run-many, affected, exec, watch, cargo, show, graph, dependencies) is admitted the same way before it starts; capacity run does it for everything else.\",\n        \"A request is admitted while the free memory stays above the floor (a share of the host memory between 4 and 8 GB), the swap stays below its ceiling and the load below its ceiling per core, the machine-wide open file table stays below its ceiling share and fewer disk images are attached than the maximum (the last three are waited out and overridden only when nothing of ours runs); memory pressure at the critical level admits nobody. Requests are served first come first served, interactive before batch.\",\n        \"The grant sets the parallelism of the selected tool through that tool's own limits: the task parallelism for Nx, the job and local-resource limits for Bazel, the core count for Cargo. SEMIO_HOST_CAPACITY=off switches the governor off explicitly.\",\n        \"Waiting prints a progress line in the chosen language and stops at the next checkpoint when the caller cancels; the grant of a process that dies is reclaimed automatically.\"\n",
+     "new": "        {\"en\": \"Every heavy repo command (run, run-many, affected, exec, watch, cargo, show, graph, dependencies) is admitted the same way before it starts; capacity run does it for everything else.\", \"de\": \"Jeder schwere repo-Befehl (run, run-many, affected, exec, watch, cargo, show, graph, dependencies) wird vor dem Start auf dieselbe Weise zugelassen; capacity run tut dies für alles andere.\"},\n        {\"en\": \"A request is admitted while the free memory stays above the floor (a share of the host memory between 4 and 8 GB), the swap stays below its ceiling and the load below its ceiling per core, the machine-wide open file table stays below its ceiling share and fewer disk images are attached than the maximum (the last three are waited out and overridden only when nothing of ours runs); memory pressure at the critical level admits nobody. Requests are served first come first served, interactive before batch.\", \"de\": \"Eine Anfrage wird zugelassen, solange der freie Speicher über der Untergrenze bleibt (ein Anteil des Host-Speichers zwischen 4 und 8 GB), der Swap unter seiner Obergrenze und die Last unter ihrer Obergrenze je Kern, die systemweite Tabelle offener Dateien unter ihrem Anteil der Obergrenze und weniger Disk-Images angehängt sind als das Maximum (die letzten drei werden abgewartet und nur übergangen, wenn nichts von uns läuft); Speicherdruck auf kritischer Stufe lässt niemanden zu. Anfragen werden in der Reihenfolge des Eintreffens bedient, interaktive vor Stapelläufen.\"},\n        {\"en\": \"The grant sets the parallelism of the selected tool through that tool's own limits: the task parallelism for Nx, the job and local-resource limits for Bazel, the core count for Cargo. SEMIO_HOST_CAPACITY=off switches the governor off explicitly.\", \"de\": \"Die Zuteilung setzt die Parallelität des gewählten Werkzeugs über dessen eigene Grenzen: die Task-Parallelität bei Nx, die Job- und lokalen Ressourcengrenzen bei Bazel, die Kernzahl bei Cargo. SEMIO_HOST_CAPACITY=off schaltet die Steuerung ausdrücklich ab.\"},\n        {\"en\": \"Waiting prints a progress line in the chosen language and stops at the next checkpoint when the caller cancels; the grant of a process that dies is reclaimed automatically.\", \"de\": \"Das Warten gibt eine Fortschrittszeile in der gewählten Sprache aus und hält am nächsten Prüfpunkt an, wenn der Aufrufer abbricht; die Zuteilung eines beendeten Prozesses wird automatisch zurückgefordert.\"}\n",
